Z||000000||86SE||08-06-2001||01:13 AM||||Between about 2000-3000 RPM a slight knock can be heard over the exhaust.  I just changed my oil today, and I just noticed the knock today.  I do throw a code 32, stupid EGR....... I am currently running 87 Regular octane.  I will switch to 92 Premium to see if it makes any difference.  The motor has 99,000 miles and the knock is kinda scareing me, i dont want to have my engine take a sh*t on me now.......<P>Thanks for any input.<BR>Chuck<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-06-2001||02:42 AM||||Uh oh...kinda sounds like good ol #4 rod bearing.<P>That's the mileage that the externally balanced(pre 88) 2.8 engines like to rattle to death.  Is this what you have..a 6cyl?<P>Does the knock increase with the rpm?  Is it a knock, ping, or rattle?  Is it there ONLY under load?<P>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||08-06-2001||03:55 AM||||It increases with RPM.  Knocks underload only slightly, with no load, big time.  Its a V6 yes.  Dosent sound good.........||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||08-06-2001||09:41 AM||||Nope, not good.<BR>My 2.8 went @ 94,000.<BR>Then I rebuilt to 3.1....and now its been swapped for 3400.<P>Whatcha gunna do?<P>Joe||||reg||9
